 {tag:'RI.2.4 Word meaning',q:'What does the word erupts mean?',a:'Bursts out',w:['Cools down','Grows taller','Falls asleep'],ev:['When magma bursts out, we say the volcano erupts'],clue:'Read the sentence with the word erupts. What does the magma do?',why:'The text says that when magma bursts out, the volcano erupts.'},
 {tag:'RI.2.1 Details',q:'What is magma called after it comes out of the ground?',a:'Lava',w:['Ash','Rock dust','Steam'],ev:['It is called lava'],clue:'Look for the words a new name.',why:'Once melted rock comes out of the ground, it is called lava.'},
 {tag:'RI.2.1 Details',q:'What is volcano ash made of?',a:'Tiny bits of rock and glass',w:['Burned-up wood and leaves','Hot drops of melted lava','Smoke from forest fires'],ev:['tiny bits of rock and glass'],clue:'Find the word ash in paragraph 3.',why:'The text says ash is made of tiny bits of rock and glass.'},
 {tag:'RI.2.2 Paragraph focus',q:'What is paragraph 4 mostly about?',a:'How volcanoes build mountains and islands',w:['Why some volcanoes stay quiet','What makes an eruption loud','Why magma rises up slowly'],ev:['That is how many volcanoes grow into tall mountains'],clue:'Paragraph 4 starts with When lava cools.',why:'Paragraph 4 tells how layers of cooled lava build mountains and islands.'},
 {tag:'RI.2.1 Details',q:'Why do scientists watch volcanoes closely?',a:'To keep people safe',w:['To make them erupt','To collect the lava','To build new islands'],ev:['Scientists who study volcanoes watch them closely to keep people safe'],clue:'Read the last sentence.',why:'The text says scientists watch volcanoes to keep people safe.'}
